Negative control for AC-4's READ half — the invoice's OWN assigned payment
method (`mapPaymentMethod`, `invoices.mappers.ts`).

Assertion it attacks: `invoices.mappers.test.ts` ›
"is the INVOICE's assigned method, not the card a payment happens to carry".

Two different records are both called `payment_details` on the wire: the
invoice's standing assignment (`raw.payment_details`) and the card one
payment happened to use (`raw.payments[].payment_details`). They are mapped by
different readers. This mutation makes the invoice's reader fall back to the
first payment's card, so an invoice with NO assigned method reports the card
of a payment already made against it — 'None selected' silently reads as
assigned, and AC-4's clear would appear not to have worked.

Re-rolled 2026-09-17 (developer, FE-3031 negative-control repair): the prior
hunk header declared a 7-line span for a 5-line body — `git apply` rejected it
as a corrupt patch. Same mutation, corrected span and context.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

